  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Country Pavillion @ the Salon international de l&#x2019;Agriculture et des Resources Animales (SARA) 2025</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The project focuses on the design and construction of a country pavilion at the Salon international de l&#x2019;Agriculture et des Resources Animales (SARA) with this year&#x2019;s theme: agrifood processing.The pavilion will showcase the Dutch capabilities in agrifood processing in the following sub-sectors:&#x2022;	Cocoa (related to combitrack; processing);&#x2022;	Horticulture (related to combitrack: route-to-market processing);&#x2022;	Cashew and mango (new market opportunities; processing); and&#x2022;	Circularity in agrifood chain (processing organic waste for bio-inputs).The stand will also play a central role at the conference for business-to-business (B2B) match making, the organisation of a networking event (drinks) where relevant African Business Partners will meet the members of the trade mission delegation, and the promotion of the Dutch companies present.15-20 Dutch companies are expected to participate in the mission.The pavilion will also provide a platform to showcase Orange Corners start-ups and ongoing Dutch programmes in C&#xf4;te d&#x2019;Ivoire.</narrative>
  </description>
